            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rationalise both fractions to obtain these forms.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{1-\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{(1+\\sqrt3)^2}{1-3}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{1-\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{4+2\\sqrt3}{-2}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{1-\\sqrt3}&=-2-\\sqrt3\\\\\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{1+\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{(1-\\sqrt3)^2}{1-3}\\\\\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{1+\\sqrt3}&=\\frac{4-2\\sqrt3}{-2}\\\\\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{1+\\sqrt3}&=-2+\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nThe rational parts are equal and the surd terms have opposite signs, so the expressions are conjugates.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
